~~~java
class Solution {
    public boolean isBalanced(TreeNode root) { return height(root) >= 0; }
    private int height(TreeNode n) {
        if (n == null) return 0;
        int l = height(n.left);
        if (l < 0) return -1;
        int r = height(n.right);
        if (r < 0 || Math.abs(l-r) > 1) return -1;
        return 1 + Math.max(l,r);
    }
}
class TreeNode {
    int val; TreeNode left,right;
    TreeNode(int val) { this.val=val; }
}
~~~
A balanced tree has child-subtree heights differing by at most one at every node. Each node is processed once: O(n) time and O(h) recursion space.

