~~~js
class Stack {
  #items = [];
  push(value) { this.#items.push(value); }
  pop() {
    if (!this.#items.length) throw new Error("Stack is empty");
    return this.#items.pop();
  }
  peek() {
    if (!this.#items.length) throw new Error("Stack is empty");
    return this.#items[this.#items.length-1];
  }
  get size() { return this.#items.length; }
}
const s=new Stack(); s.push(4); s.push(9);
console.log(s.peek()); // 9
console.log(s.pop());  // 9
~~~
The array end is the top, so each operation is amortized O(1). Empty pop/peek throw errors.

