~~~python
def binary_search(values, target):
    """Return target's index in sorted values, or -1 if absent."""
    low, high = 0, len(values) - 1
    while low <= high:
        mid = low + (high - low) // 2
        if values[mid] == target:
            return mid
        if values[mid] < target:
            low = mid + 1
        else:
            high = mid - 1
    return -1

print(binary_search([1, 3, 5, 7, 9], 7))  # 3
~~~
Input must be sorted. Each comparison halves the remaining interval, giving O(log n) time and O(1) extra space.

~~~java
public class Fibonacci {
    // F(0)=0, F(1)=1.
    public static long fibonacci(int n) {
        if (n < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("n must be nonnegative");
        if (n < 2) return n;
        long previous=0, current=1;
        for(int i=2;i<=n;i++) {
            long next=previous+current;
            previous=current; current=next;
        }
        return current;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(fibonacci(10)); // 55
    }
}
~~~
This takes O(n) time and O(1) space. long eventually overflows; use BigInteger for arbitrarily large terms.

